  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Rights Defenders Ethiopia 2020-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Civil Rights Defenders Ethiopia 2020-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Civil Rights Defenders f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;r att arbeta genom en koncentrerad insats med b&#xe5;de etablerade och nya och framtida m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttighetsorganisationer och HRD i Etiopien -- f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten f&#xf6;r denna avg&#xf6;rande civilsamh&#xe4;llsgrupp under den fortsatta demokratiska &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngen, f&#xf6;re, under och bortom de planerade nationella valen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Rights Defenders proposes to work through a concentrated effort with both established and new and up-&#xad;-coming human rights organizations and HRDs in Ethiopia -&#xad;- to strengthen the capacity of this crucial civil society group throughout the continued democratic transition, before, during and beyond the planned national elections.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this intervention has been to revitalize and strengthen human rights organizations and human rights defenders in Ethiopia through participatorydriven capacity collaboration and strengthening. To achieve this, the following mutually reinforcing pillars has been serving as sub-objectives:
1) Support in building institutional capacity
2) Strengthening security capacity
3) Increasing knowledge of and ability to advocate for human rights
4) Expanding human rights networking.

The implementation of these sub-objectives has been structured according to the following main components and expected results:
Component 1: Financial and administrative capacity strengthening
Expected results:
1. Improved understanding of financial administrative system of civil society
organizations
2. Increased overall capacity of organizations with efficient and sustainable
financial and administrative systems

Component 2: Security Capacity Strengthening
Expected results:
1. Strengthened capacity and improved knowledge of existing and emerging
HRDs on physical, psychosocial, and digital security
2. Increased ability of human rights defenders to systematically conduct human
rights monitoring and advocacy

Component 3: Strengthening human rights networking, advocacy, and
communications
Expected results:
1. Increased capacity of human rights defenders to conduct human rights
advocacy
2. Improved access to information providing better advocacy programs</narrative>
  </description>
